<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70057" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νει-όθῐ</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		Adv. (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέατος</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>at the bottom,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκεν δέ ἑ ν. θυμόν</span> it stung him
				<i>to his</i> heart's <i>core,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				567
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. λίμνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.317
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>under, beneath,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑψόθι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.355
			</span></i>; <i>in stooping posture,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.706
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. γαίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.63
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				89
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span> is rarely elided, as in
				<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				520
			</span></i>.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
